64.883616	**Correctness risks**  
64.883630	- **Race / visibility**: `staging` and `slot_ptr(slot)` may alias if slot memory is mapped into the same buffer as `staging`. Write then memcpy could corrupt the source before read.  
64.883639	- **EOF truncation**: `pread` returns `< PER_EXPERT` on short read; memcpy still copies whatever was read, leaving stale data.  
64.883640	
64.883642	**Performance risk**  
64.883643	- **Two copies**: data moves staging→staging→slot, doubling I/O and cache traffic.  
64.883644	
64.883651	**Minimal fixes**  
64.883673	- Add `if (n != PER_EXPERT) return;` after `pread`.  
64.883682	- Eliminate staging copy: `pread(fd, slot_ptr(slot), PER_EXPERT, off); slot_expert[slot]=expert_id;`
